---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { site } from '../config/site'
import '../styles/doc.css'
---

<!-- Honest statement, not a conformance claim: no formal audit has been done.
     Update the known-limitations list whenever the app changes, and never
     promise a level we have not tested. -->
<LegalLayout
  title={`Accessibility — ${site.name}`}
  description={`How accessible ${site.name} is today, the limitations we know about, and how to report a barrier.`}
  canonical={`${site.url}/accessibility`}
>
  <h1>Accessibility</h1>
  <p class="doc-meta">
    We want the game to be playable by as many people as possible. This page
    says where we are, not where we would like to be.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we stand</h2>
  <p>
    We have not completed a formal accessibility audit of the app, so we do not
    claim conformance to a standard. We aim at WCAG 2.2 level AA as the target
    and treat reported barriers as bugs, not as feature requests.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Built as plain HTML: headings in order, real links and lists, and a
      single main landmark per page.</li>
    <li>Usable with a keyboard alone, and with the browser zoomed or text
      enlarged.</li>
    <li>Text is sized in relative units and reflows down to a narrow phone
      screen.</li>
    <li>No autoplaying media, no flashing content, no pop-ups over the
      content.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The app: what we know does not work well</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The board is drawn on a canvas.</strong> A screen reader cannot
      read the checkers, points, or dice. This is the largest barrier in the
      product and the hardest to fix.</li>
    <li><strong>Some screens use a fixed layout that scales to fit.</strong>
      Increasing the system font size does not enlarge text on those screens.</li>
    <li><strong>Timed turns.</strong> Online matches give a limited time per
      move, which cannot currently be extended.</li>
    <li><strong>Colour carries meaning on the board</strong> — checker colours,
      highlights for legal moves. Board themes vary in contrast and we have not
      tested them all against a contrast standard.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What does help today</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Buttons and controls are real buttons with labels, so system settings
      such as bold text and reduced motion apply where the platform provides
      them.</li>
    <li>Legal moves are highlighted, so play never depends on remembering the
      rules or reading small print.</li>
    <li>Every legal move stays on screen until you play it, so nothing depends
      on reacting to an animation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tell us what blocks you</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>
    with the device you use, the assistive technology if any, and what you could
    not do. Reports from people who actually need the feature are worth more
    than any checklist, and they go straight onto our list.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you need this page or any of our legal documents in another format, ask
    and we will send one.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
